WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:02.709
Let's get right into audience questions today.

00:00:02.709 --> 00:00:06.470
First one is about these so-called secret
Trump voters.

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:13.630
Hey, David, I keep hearing about shy or secret
Trump voters sometimes called the silent majority.

00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:15.000
Is this really a thing?

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.570
Do the polls not understand or account for
Trump voters who simply aren't willing to

00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:23.270
say they are going to vote for Trump?

00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:29.769
So, listen, in broad strokes, the answer is
that the secret Trump voters don't really

00:00:29.769 --> 00:00:30.769
exist.

00:00:30.769 --> 00:00:36.120
There are people who point to 2016 and they
say, look, the polls were so wrong.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:40.329
People clearly weren't telling pollsters that
they were planning to vote for Donald Trump

00:00:40.329 --> 00:00:44.230
because they felt some kind of public shame
or they were embarrassed or whatever the case

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:45.230
may be.

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:47.370
The polls were basically right in 2016.

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:49.489
Hillary was winning by three in the popular
vote.

00:00:49.489 --> 00:00:55.410
She won by two point to these states, like
I believe that there was one state that really

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:59.890
was wrong, but for the most part, the battleground
states that were close, that the margins of

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:03.309
error were accounting for the actual results.

00:01:03.309 --> 00:01:07.850
So 2016 doesn't really give us evidence that
there were secret Trump voters, the idea being

00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:14.750
they hide their preference from pollsters
until they actually go out and votes.

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:25.609
A big difference between 2016 and 2020 is
that I don't know why someone would be particularly

00:01:25.609 --> 00:01:30.320
unwilling to admit today that they plan to
vote for Trump in a poll.

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:33.810
Remember this, your family, you know your
friends.

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:36.329
Nobody's going to find out how you voted in
a poll.

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:39.359
A lot of the polls now are completely automated.

00:01:39.359 --> 00:01:43.009
So it's not even that you might be embarrassed
to tell the pollster that you're planning

00:01:43.009 --> 00:01:44.319
on voting for Trump.

00:01:44.319 --> 00:01:50.259
There really would be no reason why if I got
a poll and says this is, you know, SRS press

00:01:50.259 --> 00:01:54.659
one if you plan to vote for Biden, plus press
two, if you plan to vote for Trump, why would

00:01:54.659 --> 00:01:58.590
I be shy about just answering truthfully there?

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:05.090
The only argument that could be made would
be Trump ists have coordinated to claim they

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:11.650
are voting for Biden in order to give Biden
a lead in the polls, which will motivate more

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:15.569
Trump voters to get out and vote in November.

00:02:15.569 --> 00:02:17.400
It's a complete argument.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:21.989
You know, it's a post hoc argument made to
justify something we don't actually have evidence

00:02:21.989 --> 00:02:26.319
for, and it makes no sense to me whatsoever.

00:02:26.319 --> 00:02:31.269
There were no you know, there's no evidence
that there were there are more shy Trump voters

00:02:31.269 --> 00:02:36.280
than there were shy Obama voters or shy Hillary
Clinton voters or whatever.

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:43.260
Certainly there is a significant cultural
divide in this country where there could be

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:46.579
social stigma at work from being one of the
few Trump voters.

00:02:46.579 --> 00:02:51.579
If you work at some tech firm in Austin, Texas,
a state that's likely to go to Trump, but

00:02:51.579 --> 00:02:56.350
Austin is much more blue, maybe you might
not tell your coworkers that you're going

00:02:56.350 --> 00:03:00.180
to vote for Donald Trump, but why would you
lie in a poll with your coworkers?

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:02.120
Would never know that.

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:08.730
So my sense is it's not so much that what
could turn the election would be that Trump

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:13.030
has way more support than the polls say because
of secret Trump voters.

00:03:13.030 --> 00:03:18.799
What's more likely to me is that there is
a part of the base that doesn't get involved

00:03:18.799 --> 00:03:23.250
until election time and maybe they are more
prevalent on the Republican side than the

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:24.499
Democratic side.

00:03:24.499 --> 00:03:30.569
Maybe Joe Biden's support is fully represented
in the polls, but some Trump support is still

00:03:30.569 --> 00:03:36.540
sitting out there as an, I don't know, or
third party or whatever, because people aren't

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:40.110
necessarily paying attention yet or whatever
the case may be.

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:41.970
I'm still manning the argument.

00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:46.550
I suspect that that would be a small portion
of the electorate.

00:03:46.550 --> 00:03:52.920
And I don't imagine that you are going to
see any significant amount of shy Trump supporters

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:57.780
or reticent or maybe embarrassed Trump supporters
who are going to vote for Trump in November.

00:03:57.780 --> 00:04:02.299
But for one reason or another are lying to
pollsters today.

00:04:02.299 --> 00:04:09.939
Last thought, the other argument is it's not
that there are shy Trump supporters.

00:04:09.939 --> 00:04:14.140
It's that Trump's supporters are skeptical
of polls, skeptical of polls, so they opt

00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:15.140
out.

00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:19.049
Well, the polls are normalized and adjusted
to make sure that the samples are representative.

00:04:19.049 --> 00:04:25.250
If you were, imagine that you had trouble
getting Trump supporters to respond because

00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:26.970
they hate pollsters.

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:29.520
And so you would think, oh, well, you're underrepresented.

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:31.169
Trump supporter Trump supporters in the poll.

00:04:31.169 --> 00:04:36.160
Now you just adjust and normalize the sample
to account for that.

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:41.750
And pollsters have a number of different different
methods that are scientifically, statistically

00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:42.750
acceptable.

00:04:42.750 --> 00:06:12.930
In that case, if we're wrong, then we will
know very, very soon.

